  "review_fixes": [
    "One initialization guard prevents duplicate clock handlers or time resets.",
    "Movement integrates acceleration once per frame instead of multiplying a sparse update interval by the latest speed.",
    "Combat reads the shared clock; its duplicate clock/lastFrame fields are removed.",
    "Task suspension and combat pause offsets use the same epoch as task deadlines.",
    "Path request failure deadlines cannot expire during a pause.",
    "Vanilla benchmark generation removes literal profiler-only syntax before Arma parses it.",
    "Performance validation records simulation and wall seconds separately, retaining legacy log support."
  ],
  "test_scope": "The dedicated-server accumulator tests inject pause and 5x samples into the production function; real frame sampling is tested at the server acceleration. This is not a native multiplayer pause or observed 5x client run.",
  "smoke_purpose": "Clock progress and ammo-throughput validity; no before/after performance claim."
